---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import {
	APPSUMO_PRODUCT_URL,
	APPSUMO_REVIEWS_URL,
	PRODUCT_URL,
	KEYWORDS,
	RATING_AVERAGE,
	RATING_TOTAL,
	REVIEWS_PUBLISHED,
} from "../consts";
import {
	graph,
	publisherSchema,
	websiteSchema,
	breadcrumbSchema,
} from "../lib/schema";

const structuredData = graph(
	publisherSchema(),
	websiteSchema(),
	breadcrumbSchema([
		{ name: "Home", path: "/" },
		{ name: "About", path: "/about/" },
	]),
);

const title = "Is WebAbility.io legit? Who publishes this site";
const description =
	"Who runs webabilityreviews.com, where the WebAbility.io reviews come from, and what the platform actually does. Published by the WebAbility team; reviews written by verified AppSumo purchasers.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={title}
			description={description}
			keywords={KEYWORDS.about}
			structuredData={structuredData}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About this site</h1>

			<div class="callout">
				<p>
					<strong>Disclosure.</strong> This site is published by the WebAbility
					team. We did not write the reviews. Every review here was posted by a
					verified AppSumo purchaser, and each page links back to the original so
					you can check it.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>Where the reviews come from</h2>
			<p>
				WebAbility.io holds <strong>{RATING_AVERAGE} out of 5</strong> across
				<strong>{RATING_TOTAL} verified reviews</strong> on AppSumo. This site
				reproduces <strong>all {RATING_TOTAL}</strong> of them, with a link from
				each to its original.
			</p>
			<p class="note">
				One discrepancy worth stating plainly: AppSumo's listing header currently
				reads <strong>4.9 across 26 reviews</strong>, but <strong>27</strong>
				individual reviews are live on that listing, with no duplicates. We
				publish all 27 and show the average of those 27 ({RATING_AVERAGE}).
				If AppSumo's header is the number you need, use theirs.
			</p>
			<p>
				We include the criticism as well as the praise. That means the one review
				in the set that is not five stars, the reviewer who found the widget was
				not fully translated, the reviewer whose screen reader skipped words, and
				the reviewer who could not tell that ~200 discovered fixes still needed to
				be applied. Those are in here on purpose. A page that only carried the
				good ones would not be worth reading.
			</p>
			<p>
				<a href={APPSUMO_REVIEWS_URL} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">
					Read all {RATING_TOTAL} reviews on AppSumo →
				</a>
			</p>

			<h2>What WebAbility.io is</h2>
			<p>
				WebAbility.io is a web accessibility platform. It scans a site for
				barriers in content, navigation, forms and media, automatically corrects
				the items that are safe to change — alt text, ARIA labels, contrast,
				focus order — and routes the rest to human review.
			</p>
			<p>It is built against these standards:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>ADA and WCAG 2.1 / 2.2</li>
				<li>Section 508 (US federal)</li>
				<li>AODA (Ontario)</li>
				<li>EN 301 549 (EU)</li>
				<li>IS 5568 (Israel)</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				It installs on Shopify, WordPress, Wix and Webflow, and integrates with
				GoHighLevel. Alongside the scanner there is a visitor-facing widget with
				accessibility profiles, a screen reader and controls such as text sizing.
			</p>

			<h2>A note on how to read any review page</h2>
			<p>
				Reviews carry dates, and accessibility tooling moves. The two oldest
				reviews here are from May 2025 and describe problems the later reviews do
				not mention. That does not make them wrong — it makes them a snapshot.
				Check the date on anything you read, here or anywhere else.
			</p>
			<p>
				Be equally careful with third-party "review" sites that quote monthly
				pricing tiers for this product. Those are usually affiliate pages written
				without hands-on testing, and the pricing they list does not match the
				actual listing.
			</p>

			<div class="ctas">
				<a class="btn primary" href={APPSUMO_PRODUCT_URL} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">
					See the deal on AppSumo
				</a>
				<a class="btn" href={PRODUCT_URL} rel="noopener" target="_blank">
					Visit WebAbility.io
				</a>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />

		<style>
			main {
				width: min(760px, calc(100% - 2em));
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 3em 0;
			}
			h1 {
				font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}
			h2 {
				font-size: 1.4rem;
				margin-top: 2.5rem;
			}
			.callout {
				margin: 1.5rem 0;
				padding: 1.25rem;
				border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
				border-radius: 8px;
				background: var(--gray-gradient);
			}
			.callout p {
				margin: 0;
			}
			.ctas {
				display: flex;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
				gap: 0.75rem;
				margin-top: 2.5rem;
			}
			.btn {
				display: inline-block;
				padding: 0.7rem 1.25rem;
				border-radius: 8px;
				border: 1px solid var(--accent);
				color: var(--accent);
				background: white;
				font-weight: 700;
				text-decoration: none;
			}
			.btn.primary {
				background: var(--accent);
				color: white;
			}
			.btn:hover {
				box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
